From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:33:59 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Module payloads are admitted and owned through stable leases

Module payloads hold persistent admission and kernel leases through publication, reuse and retirement, implicit module bundles are owned the same way, and an admission wait stays within the request's original deadline and is cancellable.

* feat(clangd): owned module payloads retain persistent admission and leases

* clangd: retain owned implicit module bundles through stable leases

* fix(clangd): owned worker admission waits within its original deadline

  Distinguish transient capacity pressure from identity, corruption and I/O failures. Wait outside admission locks with cancellation polling and a deadline; subtract admission time from the original worker timeout. Do not enlarge the payload quota, evict a live lease, or compile without a reservation. Concurrent publication, cancellation, timeout and invalid envelopes have real reservation controls.
